                <pb facs="0586" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg482"/>

                <head>Chapter VI: March 1–12, 1932</head>
                <p>Proclamation at Mukden of “Independent State of Manchoukuo”, March 1; Exchange of
                    Views at Shanghai on Armistice; Acceptance by China and Japan of League
                    Council’s Proposal of February 29; Meeting of Special League Assembly at China’s
                    Request, March 3; Resolution of League Assembly Calling for Cessation of
                    Hostilities at Shanghai, March 4; American Cooperation in Efforts for Peaceful
                    Settlement of Shanghai Conflict; American Consultations Respecting Threatened
                    “Independence” of Chinese Customs Administration in Manchuria; Resolution of
                    League Assembly in Reaffirmation of Treaties and of Peaceful Solution of
                    Shanghai Conflict, March 11; Statement of Approval by Secretary Stimson Concerning the Resolution of March 11;
                    Request for Recognition by “Manchoukuo”, March 12</p>

































































































































